            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "gui/gui_test/security_and_access_menu/test_sessions_sub_menu.robot",
                    "line": 153,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Keishing",
                        "email": "gkeishin@gmail.com",
                        "username": "gkeishin"
                    },
                    "message": "Sleep    capitalize it for Robot Framework keywords\n\n\nand in general using fixed sleep times makes tests slower and less reliable. The test waits 5 seconds regardless of actual page load time.  if it can be make better that would be great.\n\nExamples: \nWait Until Element Is Visible    ${xpath_sessions_sub_menu}    timeout=10s\nWait Until Element Is Visible    ${page_selection}    timeout=10s"
                },
                {
                    "file": "gui/gui_test/security_and_access_menu/test_sessions_sub_menu.robot",
                    "line": 153,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nandakumar B",
                        "email": "nandakumarb@ami.com",
                        "username": "Nandakumar-AMI"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "gui/gui_test/security_and_access_menu/test_sessions_sub_menu.robot",
                    "line": 171,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Keishing",
                        "email": "gkeishin@gmail.com",
                        "username": "gkeishin"
                    },
                    "message": "Multiple string split operations make the code harder to maintain. If the UI text format changes, multiple lines need updating.\n\n\n# Simplified approach using regex or more robust parsing something like this ? \n\nTake a look and see. \n\n${selected_count_text}=  Get Text  ${selected_count}\n# Assuming format is \"N selected\" or \"N items selected\"\n${selected_sessions}=  Fetch From Left    ${selected_count_text}    ${SPACE}\n${selected_sessions}=  Convert To Integer    ${selected_sessions}\n\nSimpler parsing logic is easier to maintain and less prone to breaking if UI text format changes slightly."
                },
